From: well0nez <8986239+well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: arm64: dts: h713: hy320: the STK8BA58 on twi1

The dtsi's accelerometer@18 (silan,sc7a20) was off on this board because
its chip is an STK8BA58. stk8ba50 drives it now (the patch before this
one): the node names "sensortek,stk8ba58". No interrupt line: the stock
tree's PB0 (stk83xx,irq-gpio <&pio 1 0 1>) stays undescribed, as the
HY310's is; h713-keystone clocks the IIO buffer with an hrtimer trigger.

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713-hy320.dts
@@ -28,8 +28,8 @@
  *    GPADC channel 1 by its gpadc node's channel_select), but with tables
  *    of another driver whose conversion is not known here.
  *  - The focus motor is disabled under stock: off here.
- *  - The accelerometer at 0x18 on twi1 is an STK8BA58 (stk,stk83xx), not
- *    the HY310's SC7A20: its node is off here.
+ *  - The accelerometer at 0x18 on twi1 is an STK8BA58 (stk,stk83xx, chip
+ *    ID 0x87), not the HY310's SC7A20: stk8ba50 drives it.
  *  - The display firmware's elog addresses, the vendor ARISC image, and no
  *    display MIPS restart (measured on the HY310 only).
  *
@@ -171,12 +171,16 @@
 
 /*
  * twi1 stays on as under stock (PH2/PH3, 100 kHz). Its chip at 0x18 is an
- * STK8BA58 (stock "stk,stk83xx", irq PB0); mainline's stk8ba50 driver is
- * for the STK8BA50, and nothing here shows the two share a register map,
- * so the dtsi's SC7A20 node is off rather than bound to the wrong chip.
+ * STK8BA58: stock "stk,stk83xx" (irq PB0), and on the unit (01.11.2026)
+ * register 0x00 reads 0x87, the vendor driver's 12-bit Sensortek ID, and
+ * the data pairs 0x02..0x07 at the reset range +-2 g (0x0f = 0x03) give a
+ * 12-bit vector of about 1020 LSB - one g at 1024 LSB/g. 0x0e (the stock
+ * tree's kxtj3) does not answer. It has the STK8BA50's register map, so
+ * stk8ba50 drives it as "sensortek,stk8ba58". No interrupt, as on the
+ * HY310: h713-keystone clocks the buffer with an hrtimer trigger.
  */
 &twi1 {
 	accelerometer@18 {
-		status = "disabled";
+		compatible = "sensortek,stk8ba58";
 	};
 };
